-- =====================================================================
-- staging_content.sql — content & reference data copied from production
--
-- NOT A MIGRATION, deliberately. Production is the SOURCE of this data,
-- so replaying it there is meaningless. This exists so a fresh
-- environment has real content to work against instead of empty tables.
--
-- EXCLUDED — member data never leaves production:
--   profiles · referrals · service_requests · suggestions
--   event_applications · notifications
--   user_contributions  (keyed on user_id)
--   nri_visits          (holds visitor names and email addresses)
--
-- support_teams.claimed_by_profile_id is nulled — those profiles do not
-- exist here, and a dangling reference is worse than an empty column.
--
-- Three things this file handles that a naive dump does not:
--   1. service_options resolves its category BY NAME. new_21 seeds the
--      same eight categories in every environment with different UUIDs,
--      so copying category_id produces a foreign-key violation.
--   2. app_settings.value is jsonb — a bare `false` is rejected.
--   3. Text is dollar-quoted. An apostrophe in an event description
--      breaks single-quoted literals.
--
-- Every statement is ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING, so it is safe to re-run.
-- Order matters: continents before countries, categories before options.
-- =====================================================================


